#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0393 expect=skipped domain=BW
#note "DISCRIMINATING. Byte-identical to -invalid_model_order-BW (columns still out of order) EXCEPT that the `#library model-column-order` line is REMOVED. getStandardModelVariables returns null for a name it holds no order for and the executor maps null AND empty to LIBRARY_NOT_AVAILABLE, so the whole rule SKIPs before the Check runs -- which is also why the rule's own `not empty($model_order)` guard is unreachable. Together with -invalid_model_order-TS this separates the two skip causes the rule used to have (class axis vs missing library metadata); after M3-D23 only this one remains."
#library standard=sendig-dart version=1-2
dataset BW class=FINDINGS label="Body Weight"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col BWSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col BWTEST   type=Char label="Body Weight Test Name"
col BWTESTCD type=Char label="Body Weight Test Short Name"
col BWORRES  type=Char label="Result or Finding in Original Units"
---
S1 | BW | 001 | 1 | Body Weight | BW | 250
S1 | BW | 002 | 1 | Body Weight | BW | 262
---
